35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The firm charges 4,200 yen hourly, billed to one person. They work around clutter, so we must tidy first.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The timing data is critical. A full pass takes one hundred and two minutes. That is over an hour of lost time.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Interesting. The kitchen data shows two or three people create most mess, while others just make coffee. The chat rows confirm disputes start with reminders about undone tasks.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,@Ryuji One hundred minutes? That’s brutal. @Benjamin So the mess is concentrated? I need to know exactly what “done” means to stop the chaos.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,@Benjamin That’s a heavy burden. @May I worry about the silence the previous tenants faced. We must protect our friendships while fixing the mess.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji One hundred minutes means 8,400 yen per visit. @Benjamin If mess is concentrated, we should price that specifically.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio That cost assumes we hire them. I need to know if rotating the duty actually removes that hour from my week, or just shifts it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji Shifting the hour is the point. If the heavy users clean, the burden matches the mess. @Toshio Pricing it specifically ignores the social cost of constant reminders.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin Exactly. If “done” means the floor and drain, not just the basin, the state stops swinging. Predictability is my priority.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,@Benjamin I agree. The previous tenants stopped speaking because of these silent resentments. We need a system that prevents that isolation.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji Shifting the hour is acceptable if the cost is shared. I need a fixed monthly figure, not variable surprises.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio Fixed figures hide the reality. I need to know if the hour disappears from my schedule, or just moves to a different day.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji The hour moves, but the load stays proportional to usage. @Toshio Fixed figures are fine, provided the baseline reflects actual kitchen activity, not just headcount.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji I need that hour gone, not just moved. @Toshio Fixed costs work, but only if the standard is clear. No more guessing.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@May I hear you. Clarity prevents resentment. @Toshio Fixed costs help, but we must ensure the arrangement keeps us talking, not just paying.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
